      "writtenOn": "2026-06-23T18:24:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would lean toward using `SkASSERT_RELEASE` here to match the Chromium guidance here: https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:styleguide/c++/c++.md;l\u003d356-372;drc\u003dbb0a8cec818c2c45184779ae0245f2b2b923f0a7\n\nIn my experience the performance hit is negligible (well-designed `CHECK`-like macros will indicate to the compiler that crashing is a cold path) and having `SkASSERT_RELEASE` has \"saved us\" by transforming what would otherwise be a security bug into a mere stability bug.\n\n(This comment also applies to one other new `SkASSERT` above)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 307,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 307,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "2287eefd9c5e10d83c11e5e6630a51d9109f36d4",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
