        "id": 8704
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-06-23T18:24:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe this is a bit silly / overboard, but would it be possible to avoid the risk of multiplication (and/or addition) overflow here somehow?  I wasn\u0027t very strict with this in my initial `SkPngRustCodec` code and it caused some preventable issues down that fuzzers found later on... :-(\n\nUsing `SkSafeMath` is one option.  Rearranging may be another (+ adding some comment).  So maybe:\n\n```suggestion\n    SkASSERT_RELEASE(fullImageBuffer.size() \u003e\u003d offset);  // Preventing subtraction underflow.\n    size_t fullRowsInFullImageBuffer \u003d (fullImageBuffer.size() - offset) / encodedRowBytes;\n    SkASSERT_RELEASE(numRows \u003e 0);  // Preventing div-by-zero and size_t-cast-overflow\n    SkASSERT_RELEASE(fullRowsInFullImageBuffer \u003e\u003d static_cast\u003csize_t\u003e(numRows));\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 603,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 604,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "2287eefd9c5e10d83c11e5e6630a51d9109f36d4",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
